WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.270
There are a few guarantees when it comes to
Deadpool: he'll word-vomit at the most inappropriate

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:09.099
times, he'll slay his enemies in ways once
thought to go against the laws of physics,

00:00:09.099 --> 00:00:13.660
and he'll make fun of anything and everything
around him, including the minds behind Marvel's

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:16.139
biggest superhero movie to date.

00:00:16.139 --> 00:00:20.040
Deadpool actor Ryan Reynolds took the opportunity
to share a message from the red-and-black

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:24.410
anti-hero, who had a few words to say about
people potentially spoiling Deadpool 2.

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:29.130
It only took fans a few seconds to realize
that the note was mostly a parody of the "Thanos

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:33.110
Demands Your Silence" initiative that Avengers:
Infinity War co-directors Joe and Anthony

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:37.610
Russo sparked up to stress the importance
of keeping plot details a secret.

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:41.460
While the Russos addressed their letter to
"the greatest fans in the world," Deadpool

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:45.859
one-upped them by opening with, "To the great-er-est
fans in the whole universe."

00:00:45.859 --> 00:00:50.329
The similarities are undeniable, with phrases
from the Russos' letter popping up verbatim

00:00:50.329 --> 00:00:54.219
in Deadpool's note, but most of Deadpool's
comments added a ridiculous twist.

00:00:54.219 --> 00:00:58.590
For example, one of the "super secrets" his
team has been hiding is the, quote, "secret

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:02.280
blend of 11 herbs and spices in Colonel Sanders'
delicious moustache."

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:08.540
After telling people not to "say a f---ing
word about the fun s--- in the movie," Deadpool

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:15.070
signed off with a hashtag of his own: #WadeWilsonDemandsYourSisterSorryStupidAutocorrectSilence.

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:17.090
And now, the Russo brothers have something
to say.

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:21.390
Replying to Reynolds on Twitter, the directors
fired back with a photo of a prop Infinity

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:24.000
Gauntlet with its middle finger raised, captioned:
"Boom."

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.720
"Pump the hate brakes, Thanos."

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:30.320
Reynolds was quick to respond to the flip
of the bird, though this time, he took a higher

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:33.300
road than Deadpool would have, replying, "I
deserve that."

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:37.259
All things considered, it's safe to assume
that the Russos aren't actually angry, and

00:01:37.259 --> 00:01:41.310
that the minds behind the Deadpool sequel
don't actually think the Russos' anti-spoiler

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:43.270
attitude is in any way uncool.

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:44.270
How could they?

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:48.729
Infinity War has continued to smash records
at the box office, surpassing the $1 billion

00:01:48.729 --> 00:01:54.150
benchmark in record time, and Deadpool 2 first
reactions stamp the sequel film as being bigger,

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:56.670
better, and more brilliant than the original.

00:01:56.670 --> 00:02:00.340
Something tells us both parties are too busy
basking in their respective successes to be

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:01.990
truly fired up.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:02.990
Thanks for watching!

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:05.149
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:02:05.149 --> 00:02:07.070
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

